<title>CANADA: Wascana Energy sets rights separation date.</title>
<headline>Wascana Energy sets rights separation date.</headline>
<dateline>REGINA, Saskatchewan 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wascana Energy Inc, target of a C$1.7 billion takeover bid from Talisman Energy Inc, said on Monday that its board of directors set the separation date for rights issued under its shareholder rights plan at March 21.</p>
<p>Wascana said the separation of &quot;poison pill&quot; rights from the company's common shares could also be moved to a later date if its board so determined.</p>
<p>Talisman's offer for the Regina-based oil producer expires on March 24 and Wascana's directors were expected to make a recommendation to shareholders by March 13.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
